cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SE Inspect, VORSA-M3 or the published measurements, please cite this repository."
title: "SE Inspect (VORSA INSPECT): a neuromorphic inspection cell on Raspberry Pi 5 with BrainChip AKD1500"
authors:
  - family-names: Thurmayr
    given-names: Andreas
    affiliation: "SpikingEdge (independent)"
version: "1.0.0-alpha.1"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
license: "PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0"
url: "https://spikingedge.com/projects/vorsa-inspect/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Acinger/SpikingEdge-Inspect"
keywords:
  - neuromorphic
  - Akida
  - AKD1500
  - on-chip learning
  - Raspberry Pi 5
  - industrial inspection
  - edge AI
abstract: >-
  An inspection cell that learns new parts on the AKD1500 in seconds, classifies by
  aligned silhouettes, measures parts geometrically on the Raspberry Pi and reports
  "unknown" rather than guessing. Every published figure carries its date, build,
  firmware and method; benches in tools/ reproduce the synthetic results without hardware.
